1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320392/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8bd562a1-de76-57bf-8a2a-0fff1c9df0c4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-320392/field-1/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" :answer-field/choices ["q-320392/field-1/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-320392" :question/id #uuid "5b426326-b653-592b-bbad-842bee9a0bbe" :question/math-academy-id "q-320392" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979011/assets/6881c7b52de83103dcfc483ec25455781a4d399653e2369d28f6924327f8ee56.png)\n\nDetermine the area $A$ of the parallelogram in the figure.\n\n$\\,\\,A=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we get the vectors\n\n$$\n\\text{u}=⟨-3,2⟩,\\,\\text{v}=⟨1,3⟩.\n$$\n\nFirst, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-9-2 \\\\  & =-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|-11|=11\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-320392/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "288e49b0-f706-54de-86b7-a17248fe2408"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-320392"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-320401/field-1/abe476e447976564bc5c670fe73789666287b967d49bbed12b1d85144449e63e" :answer/id #uuid "da7c3e53-ea11-5924-9681-c7c3af69e697" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "23" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320401/field-1/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "2e542d75-809e-5364-be9a-26a2da8cac97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320401/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d3cd4ea3-2e9a-5c48-9e8a-2b1b46dba0e9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-320401/field-1/abe476e447976564bc5c670fe73789666287b967d49bbed12b1d85144449e63e" :answer-field/choices ["q-320401/field-1/abe476e447976564bc5c670fe73789666287b967d49bbed12b1d85144449e63e" "q-320401/field-1/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-320401" :question/id #uuid "6a665495-2aa5-5e3c-af99-7d30a1a81b07" :question/math-academy-id "q-320401" :question/problem "Determine the area $A$ of the parallelogram spanned by $\\text{u}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $\\text{v}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$\n\n$\\,\\,A=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot 4-5\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-8-15 \\\\  & =-23\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|\\,-23\\,|=23\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-320401/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "288e49b0-f706-54de-86b7-a17248fe2408"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-320401"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-320553/field-1/3c2d07bc9e5fa6937479c926df84e1f97dcbe3977ab8ed6f3b108b1a2a3e55f2" :answer/id #uuid "c6eb67d7-299b-5f9f-a3d8-3596447fb4ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{12}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320553/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "0001203e-7ac4-51ba-958e-a15e910eb722" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-320553/field-1/3c2d07bc9e5fa6937479c926df84e1f97dcbe3977ab8ed6f3b108b1a2a3e55f2" :answer-field/choices ["q-320553/field-1/3c2d07bc9e5fa6937479c926df84e1f97dcbe3977ab8ed6f3b108b1a2a3e55f2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-320553" :question/id #uuid "ec8978a8-907e-5a48-8bc8-078b7ba83da1" :question/math-academy-id "q-320553" :question/problem "Given that the area spanned between the vectors $\\text{u}=⟨-\\frac{4}{3},7⟩$ and $\\text{v}=⟨a,-9⟩$ equals zero, what is the value of $a?$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{3} & a \\\\ 7 & -9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{3} & a \\\\ 7 & -9\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-\\frac{4}{3})\\cdot (-9)-a\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =12-7a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, setting the expression for the determinant equal to $0$ and solving for $a,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12-7a & =0 \\\\ 7a & =12 \\\\ a & =\\frac{12}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-320553/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0272b8d6-8400-5a6d-b51d-fc6ca84bd166"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-320553"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
